The layers, and the one direction they point
Seven bands, stacked. Outside the container sit the operator, the fleet
reader and the verifier. Below them the composition layer brings a tenant up
and mounts every door; then doors and guards, which are the tenant's
authority, the personal-data membrane and the audit and write discipline;
then work and participation, which is runs, lanes, streams, sync and
subscriptions; then the faces, each a version personality over one shared
implementation; then the engine, which knows objects, envelopes, identity and
the outbox and nothing about FHIR or any framework. A last band holds what is
installed everywhere and may be named by anything: the promises, telemetry
and logging. Every arrow points down.
